What is null_resource in Terraform?

Sometimes in Terraform, we need to run a custom script or a command — like installing a package or copying a file — but there’s no direct Terraform block for that.
That’s where null_resource comes in.
 It lets you run manual commands using local-exec (runs locally) or remote-exec (runs on a server via SSH).


Real Example:
You created a VM with Terraform and now want to:
Copy a .env file to it
Install some software
Restart the app
Terraform can’t do this directly. So we use null_resource with remote-exec to run these commands after the VM is created.

This is very useful when:
     You want to automate post-deployment tasks
     There's no direct Terraform support
     You want quick scripts to run inside your IaC flow


Important:
 Don’t overuse null_resource. Use it only when you really need custom logic.
